// ---- src/diagrams/cartography/contour-lines.js ----
// Diagram "contour-lines": from relief to contour lines, the static version of the sim "contour-lines", for print.
// A synthetic landscape inspired by the Creux du Van (Jura, Neuchâtel), 4 km × 3 km: a valley, a forested flank,
// a plateau that rises gently to a summit and a cirque cut into it, closed by a cliff. Above, the landscape in
// relief (heights exaggerated) cut by horizontal planes every 100 m; below, the map with the contour lines, the same
// x; dashed lines drop from the cuts to the contour lines. On the right, the profile along A–B (through the cirque)
// and the five things to read: summit, gentle slope, cliff, steep slope, valley.
