// ---- src/diagrams/cartography/true-size.js ----
// Diagram "true-size": the static version of the sim of the same name, for print. A Mercator world map (58° S – 84° N)
// with Greenland, Africa and Russia at their real place, and copies of Greenland and Russia moved to the equator: on the
// globe they keep their shape and size, on the map they shrink to their true size. Greenland looks as big as Africa,
// which is 14 times bigger.
//   <div class="geores" data-diagram="true-size"></div>
//   data-title="false": no title (on a slide, which has its own)
// Data: dist/countries.js (Natural Earth 1:50m).
//
// R_.trueSize: the geometry shared with the sim: countries as unit vectors, their area on the sphere, their centre,
// the rotation that moves a country on the globe and the area of its picture on Mercator's map.
